EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: Caddy 2.8.4 applies stream-reset rate-limit — all required assumptions are refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: caddy:2.8.4
TARGET_PORT: 443/udp
CLIENT_TOOL: aioquic

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent rapid RESET_STREAM frames against caddy:2.8.4 HTTP/3 endpoint.
  After ~200 resets/s the server sent QUIC GOAWAY and closed the connection.
  CPU stayed below 5% throughout. Memory delta < 3 MB. No server-side resource
  accumulation observed. Caddy 2.8.4 introduced a stream-churn rate limit
  (default 200/s) in response to CVE-2023-44487 disclosures.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A3 ("no stream-churn rate limit") is refuted. The patch
                applies to HTTP/3 as well as HTTP/2 in Caddy 2.8.x.
